<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-S3-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-S3-001" ;
  triage:title "signal_hook::iterator::Signals used inside #[cfg(windows)] block — E0432 Windows CI compile error (lifecycle_control.rs:195)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/lifecycle_control.rs:195 — signal_hook::iterator::Signals is used inside a #[cfg(windows)] code block, but signal_hook::iterator is cfg(all(not(windows), feature=\"iterator\")) and is unavailable on Windows. This produces E0432: unresolved import signal_hook::iterator on Windows CI. Fix: replace with signal_hook::flag::register(SIGINT, terminate.clone()) which is available on all platforms. Fix together with ATM-QA-S3-002 (WIN-RELOAD-001) — same commit, same function. (quality-mgr reported as CI-BLOCK-001-S3 in S.3 QA-2 report.)" ;
  triage:category "ATM-QA" ;
